Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/os/FileUtils.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0), framework
breadth F2: convertToModernFd answers null.

Why: convertToModernFd asks MediaProvider (MediaStore.getOriginalMediaFormatFileDescriptor) whether a file descriptor
has an unredacted twin, and answers null when it has none or the provider cannot be reached, which ExifInterface,
MediaMetadataRetriever and others then take as "use the descriptor given". Minato has no MediaProvider and
MediaStore is a stub, so the call would end in a NoClassDefFoundError that its catch of Exception does not catch.
The answer null is the one Android gives an app whose file the media provider does not redact.

